%N A398213 Decimal expansion of the midradius of a canonical (dual-uniform) octagonal trapezohedron with unit short edge length.
%C A398213 The octagonal trapezohedron is the dual polyhedron of the octagonal antiprism.
%H A398213 Paolo Xausa, <a href="/A398213/b398213.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%H A398213 David I. McCooey, <a href="https://dmccooey.com/polyhedra/OctagonalTrapezohedron.html">Octagonal Trapezohedron</a>.
%H A398213 Polytope Wiki, <a href="https://polytope.miraheze.org/wiki/Octagonal_antitegum">Octagonal antitegum</a>.
%H A398213 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/Trapezohedron.html">Trapezohedron</a>.
%H A398213 <a href="/index/Al#algebraic_08">Index entries for algebraic numbers, degree 8</a>.
%F A398213 Equals csc(Pi/16)*sqrt(1 + 2*cos(Pi/8))/4 = csc(Pi/16)*sqrt(1 + A179260)/4.
%F A398213 Equals the largest real root of 512*x^8 - 2560*x^6 + 768*x^4 + 32*x^2 - 1.
%e A398213 2.1624989466365142756191829571083252557786422867751...
%t A398213 First[RealDigits[Csc[Pi/16]*Sqrt[1 + 2*Cos[Pi/8]]/4, 10, 100]]
%t A398213 (* Alternative: *)
%t A398213 First[RealDigits[PolyhedronData[{"Trapezohedron", 8}, "Midradius"], 10, 100]]
%Y A398213 Cf. A398210 (volume), A398211 (surface area), A398212 (inradius), A398214 (height).
%Y A398213 Cf. A398215 (long edge).
%Y A398213 Cf. A398216 (small face angle), A398217 (large face angle), A398218 (dihedral angle).
%Y A398213 Cf. A394536 (midradius of the dual).
%Y A398213 Cf. A179260.
